diff --git a/doc/source/admin/instance-checkpoints.rst b/doc/source/admin/instance-checkpoints.rst
index 4ac0922..01ff250 100644
--- a/doc/source/admin/instance-checkpoints.rst
+++ b/doc/source/admin/instance-checkpoints.rst
@@ -31,9 +31,9 @@ readiness evidence. Previously admitted work remains protected when disabled.
        resize/confirm/revert, live migration/abort/force-complete,
        evacuate, shelve/offload/unshelve
      - Quota, placement, storage/network preparation or task dispatch
-     - Ordinary claim before method body and validation callbacks. Live
+     - Pure API validators run before acquiring the ordinary claim. Live
        checkpoints reject topology changes. Existing pending task states remain
-       additional admission barriers.
+       additional admission barriers. The claim still precedes mutation/I/O.
    * - Compute API start/stop/reboot, pause/unpause, suspend/resume,
        image snapshot/backup, crash dump, lock/unlock, network-info injection
      - State update, Glance image creation or compute RPC
@@ -72,6 +72,17 @@ readiness evidence. Previously admitted work remains protected when disabled.
      - Thread-pool submission, then migration driver
      - Explicit handoff to ``_do_live_migration`` before submission; the worker
        adopts before effects. Submission failure retains the queued claim.
+   * - Live-migration abort/force-complete
+     - Existing migration control RPC and driver call
+     - A separate durable control token is bound to the primary owner,
+       migration UUID and source endpoint. It pins the primary until both
+       workers finish; unknown control outcomes retain both claims. Successful
+       cancellation of a queued Future closes ownership only after cleanup.
+   * - API DB InstanceMapping changes and deletion, including bulk deletion
+     - Cell routing or mapping deletion
+     - Ticket reservation and mapping mutation lock the same mapping row.
+       Held/confirmed tickets prevent moves or deletion until cell cancellation
+       or resource-deletion proof permits refund. No cell call holds this lock.
    * - Cell DB Instance/BDM/VIF/ShareMapping/InstanceExtra/info-cache writers
      - SQL mutation
      - Same writer transaction locks Instance first. Matching durable scope is
@@ -90,7 +101,9 @@ cell record, token, action and generation to match. Checkpoint writes additional
 require a matching claimed phase; only runtime state or reconnection bookkeeping
 is writable, never the protected device identity.
 
-Ordinary failures after acquisition retain the claim for investigation. N1
+Ordinary failures after acquisition retain the claim for investigation. Pure
+validation rejections do not acquire an owner. Checkpoint conflicts on ordinary
+HTTP APIs return 409, including old microversions. N1
 provides no automatic unlock or ordinary-worker takeover. Cross-cell workflows
 retain their native pending/resize states and API mapping protocol in addition
 to local claims; a copied Instance row is not a transferable checkpoint owner.
@@ -155,7 +168,8 @@ before quota readiness. Request UUID reuse is scoped to project and server;
 the actor, action and canonical payload must also match. Authorization is
 checked again on every replay.
 
-Cancellation writes a durable cell tombstone before refunding the ticket.
+Cancellation writes a durable cell tombstone before refunding the ticket,
+including when the Instance has already been deleted or purged.
 Late admission of that operation is then fenced. Delete and completed create
 cleanup release usage only after a durable cell proof that all owned resources
 are gone. A timeout, missing reply, down cell or one ``operation not found``
